Data: any random facts about anything
Information: related data for a thing

Program / software : set of instructions/code with data to run and provide desired result
Process: running program



Data Structure: way of organizing data in computer's memory so that it can be used efficiently by program code.

DBMS: data structure where data is getting arranged and stored in harddisk for storing purpose

hdd: hard disk drive
ssd: solid state drive (new)



Algorithm: Process or set of rules followed in calculation or solving other solutions

Properties of Algorithm:
    input: (optional) given data to the algorithm to work the process on
    output: (must) result -> to diaplay / to be stored / to pass to next algorithm
    definiteness: the steps should be clear to understand
    finiteness: (should not be infinite) finite number of steps




Pseudocode: (false code) (not run by computer) (human readable) (no standard syntax) used to write algorithm steps with plain language
Example of pseudocode:
    problem/purpose: find the sum of two numbers
    name: sum
        sum(a,b):
            1. input a, b
            2. sum <- a + b
            3. display sum

Drawbacks of pseudocode:
    can not be understandable by all
    can not be shared
    not fully clear communication on steps
    language dependent


Flowchart: diagrammatic representation of an algorithm
    American National Standard Institute (ANSI) set the standards for flowcharts and their symbols in the 1960s
    human reading not machine reading
